Animate the Object Camera
You can animate the camera on a camera animation path of the selected Frame, thus creating the
impression of flying through the scene.
Note
You have to define a camera animation path on the Tab Camera Animation of the respective Frame.
To move the animation camera:
• Change to the View ribbon tab and click Animate.
• Select the name of the animation path for the selected object in the dialog Fly on Path or for the root
object of the scene from the list Path Name [MU animation].
• Select Backwards if you want the camera to move backward toward the starting point of the animation
path. Plant Simulation automatically enters a negative velocity into the text box when you select the
check box.
• To start the animation, click Play 
 .
Animate the Object Camera
10-908 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

3D now shows the scene through the lens of the animation camera, which moves on the path you
designated with a lens offset of (0, 0, 0.1).
• To pause the animation of the camera, independent of the simulation, click Pause 
 .
• To stop the animation of the camera, independent of the simulation, click Stop 
 .
At the end of the animation 3D sets the main camera to the last point where the animation camera was
located and deletes the animation camera.
To test the camera animation path you defined, click the tab Test in the dialog Edit Path, select an
Animated graphic, and start the test animation.
Compare Work with Animation Paths
