Controlling Your View in the Scene
Control Your View
The 3D window provides several ways of setting how you look at the scene, i.e., of controlling the camera
that represents the eyes of the viewer looking at the scene.
You can:
• Set the Main Directions
• Set View Points
• Attach a Camera to an Object/Frame and Detach it
• Animate the Camera
Back to Visualizing the Material Flow
Set the Main Directions
Independent of the active camera setting, you can adjust the view to any main direction of the view or of
an object at any time.
When you selected an object, the 3D window zooms out this object and adapts the direction of the camera
to the selected main direction of the coordinate system of the object.
Compare Align the View to the Main Directions
Controlling Your View in the Scene
Plant Simulation Help 10-909
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Control Your View
Set View Points
You can save any view of the scene, i.e., the position and orientation of the main camera within the scene,
at any time, and return to this view later on.
You can also save the active camera setting, together with the active root object of the scene, with a
meaningful name as one of the Camera Marks 
 .
As opposed to the view points that 3D saves automatically, you can save any number of Camera Marks,
which it saves in the model file. You can then rename and delete them at will.
Back to Control Your View
Attach a Camera to an Object/Frame and Detach it
You can attach a camera to any object, so that you can view the scene through the lens of this object, and
detach a camera from it again, when you do not need it any more. When the object moves through the
scene, for example because you started the simulation, the camera will move along with the object you
attached it to.
In addition, Plant Simulation:
• Visualizes the camera you attached, i.e., inserts an animatable object that represents the camera.
• Enables you to change between object view and normal view.
• Enables you to manually transform the camera you attached: By changing the view while in object view,
or by manipulating the object, while in normal view.
• Enables you to set the speed and the direction of the animation.
Set View Points
10-910 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Enables you to pause, continue, and stop the camera animation independent of other animations and
simulations.
Compare Attach a Camera to an Object
Compare Detach the Camera from an Object
Back to Control Your View
Animate the Camera
You can make the camera move on any animation path of the selected object or of the root object of the
scene. Here, you fly on this path and view the scene from it.
In addition, Plant Simulation:
• Visualizes the animated camera, i.e., inserts an animatable object that represents the camera.
• Enables you to change between animation view and normal view during the animation.
• Enables you to manually transform the animated camera: By changing the view while in animation view,
or by manipulating the object, while in normal view.
• Enables you to define the speed of the animation and the direction of the animation.
• Enables you to pause, continue and stop the camera animation, independent of other animations and
simulations.
Compare Animate the Object Camera
Compare Fly on a Defined Path Through the Scene
