Working with the Grid
Work with the Grid
Plant Simulation uses the grid as the surface onto which it inserts objects.
Animate the Camera
Plant Simulation Help 10-911
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Be aware that showing or hiding the grid affects how objects behave:
• When you show the grid, manipulating objects always refers to the grid plane.
• When you hide the grid, manipulating objects refers to your view plane, i.e., the plane perpendicular to
the direction in which you look at the scene.
To change and define grid settings for the current simulation model and to open the dialog Edit Grid and
Base Plate Settings, click Settings 
  on the View ribbon tab.
To change the grid settings for new models, select File > Preferences > 3D [preferences].
The grid in the 3D window looks like this. The origin of the grid is located in the top left corner of the
window offset by one grid unit to the right and down each.
Plant Simulation re-creates the grid after each change you make in the model when it redraws the scene.
So, when you insert and move an object toward the borders of the grid, it automatically extends in that
direction. The grid always expands or shrinks to show all objects in the scene.
As the grid is intended to be a modeling help when creating the model, you will usually hide it when
presenting your model. To do so, press the Ins key on the keyboard.
Plant Simulation adjusts the dimensions and the borders of the grid to the position of the objects shown in
the scene.
Work with the Grid
10-912 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The origin of the grid, i. e., the lines that are red by default, always are part of the grid.
The grid size always is a multiple of the smallest visible grid distance.
You can:
• Show and Hide the Grid
• Set Grid Properties
• Edit Grid Lines
• Position the Grid on Different Planes
• Move the Grid in the Window
After you inserted objects into your simulation model, you can align them to the grid 
 , make
them snap to the grid 
 , make them snap to other objects 
 , or arrange them on the grid.
To be able to do so, make sure that Show Grid 
  is on.
Back to Visualizing the Material Flow
Show and Hide the Grid
You can show or hide the grid in the 3D window containing your simulation models.
Show and Hide the Grid
