• To assign a color to the coordinate axes, consisting of the x-axis and the y-axis, click the arrow in of the
drop-down list Axes Color and select a color.
• To define the settings of the grid lines, edit them in the table on the tab.
Set Grid Properties
10-914 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Work with the Grid
Edit Grid Lines
You can edit existing grid lines or add new grid lines.
You do this in the group box Grid Lines.
• To add another grid line, click Add.
Enter the distance between two grid lines, which you want to add; we entered 2 meters.
Select a color for the grid line, we selected a bright blue.
Edit Grid Lines
Plant Simulation Help 10-915
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• To show this grid line in the grid in the scene, select Visible.
• Then, select if objects you insert snap to this grid line. Making objects snap to grid points enables you
to precisely place objects with the mouse.
• To edit an existing grid line, select it in the list and edit the distance between the grid lines, their color,
what objects, which you insert, snap to, and if this grid line is visible or not.
Back to Work with the Grid
Position the Grid on Different Planes
You can display the grid on the different planes in three-dimensional space.
As you remember Plant Simulation uses a left-handed coordinate system.
The x-axis runs from left-to-right, the z-axis runs from bottom-to-top, and the y-axis runs from front-to-
back.
• To place the grid on the planes defined by the axes, click Transform 
  on the View ribbon tab
and select the respective radio button in the dialog Grid Position and Orientation.
Position the Grid on Different Planes
10-916 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
Plant Simulation does not save the settings you select in this dialog. They only apply as long as the
dialog is open.
To position the grid on the plane defined by the x-
axis and the y-axis, select Orientation > XY Plane.
To position the grid on the plane defined by the x-
axis and the z-axis, select Orientation > XZ Plane.
To position the grid on the plane defined by the y-
axis and the z-axis, select Orientation > YZ Plane.
Back to Work with the Grid
Move the Grid in the Window
You can move the origin of the grid in the window of your simulation model.
Move the Grid in the Window
Plant Simulation Help 10-917
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To do so, click Transform 
  on the View ribbon tab and roll the mouse wheel in the text boxes and
click the buttons below Position in the dialog Grid Position and Orientation.
Note
3D does not save the settings you select in this dialog. They only apply as long as the dialog is open.
Note
When moving the origin of the grid, Plant Simulation uses the length unit you selected under Model
Settings > Units > Length.
• To move the position of the Origin of the grid on the x-axis by
0.01 length units to the right, click in the text box, hold down Ctrl, and roll the mouse wheel forward.
0.1 length units to the right, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel forward.
1 length unit to the right, click in the text box, hold down Shift, and roll the mouse wheel forward.
0.01 length units to the left, click in the text box, hold down Ctrl, and roll the mouse wheel backward.
0.1 length units to the left, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel backward.
1 length unit to the left, click in the text box, hold down Shift, and roll the mouse wheel backward.
• To move the position of the Origin of the grid on the y-axis by
0.01 length units to the back, click in the text box, hold down Ctrl, and roll the mouse wheel forward.
0.1 length units to the back, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel forward.
1 length unit to the back, click in the text box, hold down Shift, and roll the mouse wheel forward.
0.01 length units to the front, click in the text box, hold down Ctrl, and roll the mouse wheel backward.
0.1 length units to the front, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel backward.
Move the Grid in the Window
10-918 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

1 length unit to the front, click in the text box, hold down Shift, and roll the mouse wheel backward.
• To move the position of the Origin of the grid on the z-axis by
0.01 length units up, click in the text box, hold down Ctrl, and roll the mouse wheel forward.
0.1 length units to the up, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel forward.
1 length unit to the up, click in the text box, hold down Shift, and roll the mouse wheel forward.
0.01 length units to the down, click in the text box, hold down Ctrl, and roll the mouse wheel
backward.
0.1 length units to the down, click in the text box and roll the mouse wheel backward.
1 length unit to the down, click in the text box, hold down Shift, and roll the mouse wheel backward.
• To reset the values for the x-axis, the y-axis and the z-axis to their predefined default values of 0, 0, 0,
click Scene Origin.
• To set the values for the x-axis, the y-axis and the z-axis to the values of the position of a single object
you selected, click Object Origin.
